  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish has a few irregular verbs whose present tense forms do not follow regular patterns.\nThe verbs 'ir' (to go), 'dar' (to give) and 'ver' (to see) have unique 1st person singular forms (voy, doy, veo) and distinct forms for each person. Learning these forms is essential for everyday conversation."
